**Definition 158.1 (Vertex and intersection conventions).** The eight
initial ordered-simplex vertices are $v^0=0$ and
$v^k=(1,\ldots,1,0,\ldots,0)$ with $k$ initial ones, $1\le k\le7$.
Starting with rows 0--7, intersect successively with rows 8 through 74.
At each stage sort the distinct vertices lexicographically in their seven
rational coordinates, and number them from zero. For a new row let
$s(u)=b_h-A_hu$ be its slack. A crossing edge is recorded as $(i,j)$,
where the old vertex $u_i$ has positive slack and $u_j$ negative slack.
Its intersection point is

$$
\frac{s(u_i)u_j-s(u_j)u_i}{s(u_i)-s(u_j)}.
\tag{158.1}
$$

